      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg per day. At that dose the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and shock. Overdoses of this size have caused prolonged, hard-to-treat cardiovascular collapse. Normal kidney and liver function don't change that.\n\nYou also mentioned you aren't a clinician. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient.\n\n- **If 50 mg was a typo,** the usual adult dose is 5 mg once daily, and it can be raised to 10 mg. Tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it. Starting doses are often 2.5 mg for frail or older patients.\n- **If a prescriber really intended 50 mg,** they should confirm the dose directly with pharmacy and enter or co-sign the order themselves.\n\nWhich dose do you want, or who is the prescriber I should route this to?"
      }
