     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 50 mg of amlodipine daily is five times the maximum dose and could seriously harm the patient. A non-prescriber also can't authorize it.\n\nHere are the options that would work:\n\n- **Prescriber review:** The treating physician or another licensed prescriber can review the case. If they think a dose that high is justified, they can enter the order themselves and talk to pharmacy first.\n- **A different dose:** If the goal is blood pressure control, I can enter amlodipine at a standard dose of 2.5 to 10 mg once daily. I'll need the prescriber to specify which one.\n- **Pharmacy or the on-call physician:** If you're worried about the patient's blood pressure now, they can advise quickly.\n\nTell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
